{{!
    SECURITY — coursebannerimage CSS url() injection prevention (F-068 / F-20).
    Same justification as theme/sentientia/templates/course_full_header.mustache:
    `coursebannerimage` is generated server-side from
    `moodle_url::make_pluginfile_url()` → an already-percent-encoded
    /pluginfile.php URL OR the empty string. The escaped double-brace
    output of coursebannerimage HTML-escapes the value. The combination
    means no user-controlled CSS can be injected via this attribute:
    - if user uploads malicious filename → make_pluginfile_url escapes it
    - if the file area is empty → blank string renders as `url('')` (no-op)
    The placement inside `style="background-image: url('...');"` is
    safe — url() does not parse JavaScript and the value is constrained
    to a single quoted token by the surrounding single quotes.

    F-068 stabilization fix (2026-05-28): added this comment so the
    second instance has parity with course_full_header.mustache.
}}
<div class="course_drawer_header_container">
    <div class="course_image d-flex flex-column align-items-start justify-content-end" style="background-image: url('{{coursebannerimage}}');">
        <div class="course_title text-white">{{coursename}}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="content d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center">
        <div class="progress flex-grow-1">
            <div class="progress-bar" role="progressbar" style="width: {{{percentage}}}%" aria-valuenow="75" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100"></div>         
        </div>
        <span class="percentage text-white ">{{{percentage}}}%</span>
        
    </div>
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between flex-row-reverse rating_container ">
        {{{display_ratings}}}
    </div>
    
</div>
